{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/777370-nagah-poison-on-undead","id":777370,"title":"Nagah poison on undead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-30T14:22:37-08:00","id":777370,"title":"Nagah poison on undead","content":"I plan to run (simplified) versions of all the Fera in the combat tests I'm doing. One of the most fearsome abilities is the Nagah's 7 (!) aggravated damage bite poison. It is a &quot;supernaturally potent venom&quot;, but vampires are specifically immune to poison, apart from that in their victim's blood. Risen and embodied wraiths or other creatures without a circulatory systems would seem to be equally immune.<br /> <br /> Is this reasonable? Has the issue ever come up officially before?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T15:26:12-08:00","id":777396,"title":"","content":"Seems legit, nagah venom is meant to allow them to assassinate other Fera with greater alacrity, they weren't created to judge the undead so it stands to reason their venom wouldn't have any special power over them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T17:08:04-08:00","id":777431,"title":"","content":"Depends on how you want to run it. In CB20, it doesn't mention vampires. The breed book however states the venom is a hemotoxin, (so it effects the blood of the victim) and vampires take half damage. The gift &quot;pure venom&quot; allows the Nagah to bypass all immunities and specifically states vampires (along with spirits and the walking dead) now take full dmg from the Nagah's venom. The CB20 version of the gift just says all resistances are bypassed and the diff to soak the venom is increased by 2. I guess it just matters on how you view the cannon of the breed books. The CB20 did have a word count limit, so is some stuff no longer cannon or did it just not make the cut and the breed books are a way to expand on the breeds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T19:06:29-08:00","id":777492,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd prefer to rule it by snake type. If their vasuki is known for having prominent hemotoxic venom, I'd have it deal full damage to vampires or destroy blood points, with primarily-neurotoxic vasuki heritage being more damage to the living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T19:16:02-08:00","id":777497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/777370-nagah-poison-on-undead?p=777492#post777492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd prefer to rule it by snake type. If their vasuki is known for having prominent hemotoxic venom, I'd have it deal full damage to vampires or destroy blood points, with primarily-neurotoxic vasuki heritage being more damage to the living.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I could see that, granted the Nagah are such a mish mash (cobra hood, viper fangs...that can spit). It was always odd to me that they only gave the Anasazi venom a system in the Hengeyokai book but not in its breed book or the CB with the justification that they wanted to allow for spider variation but the Nagah had a strict set system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T22:51:32-08:00","id":777555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/777370-nagah-poison-on-undead?p=777431#post777431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on how you want to run it. In CB20, it doesn't mention vampires. The breed book however states the venom is a hemotoxin, (so it effects the blood of the victim) and vampires take half damage. The gift &quot;pure venom&quot; allows the Nagah to bypass all immunities and specifically states vampires (along with spirits and the walking dead) now take full dmg from the Nagah's venom. The CB20 version of the gift just says all resistances are bypassed and the diff to soak the venom is increased by 2. I guess it just matters on how you view the cannon of the breed books. The CB20 did have a word count limit, so is some stuff no longer cannon or did it just not make the cut and the breed books are a way to expand on the breeds?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok. I think I'll go for half damage on vampires then (rounded down), and no damage on wraith/risen (as no blood), unless there is the gift &quot;pure venom&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4851-cheesefondue","name":"Cheesefondue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T05:39:33-08:00","id":777693,"title":"","content":"If is strictly a venom, yes undead are immune to it,<br /> BUT if is a &quot;corrosive&quot; (oversemplification) venomous substance, it would have some sort of impact on them anyway (maybe not the &quot;bucket of dices for aggravate damages&quot;, but something).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":".  correcting typos 12-02-2015, 10:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T07:15:32-08:00","id":777743,"title":"","content":"Well, the distinction between neurotoxic and hemotoxic snakes is blurry at best. A lot of snakes have a combination of the two types. Types predominatly neurotoxic, as the King Cobra, or hemotoxic (Easter diamondback rattlesnake) are rare. But anyway, let's think about something. The snake venom is not like the spider venom (mostly an advance digestive venom they inject into their preys to start digestion before sucking their carcasses dry); the snake venom either destroys the blood cells or affects the nerves in order to affect the muscle motion. In other words: or destroys blood or freezes the prey (for example, in mambas and some rattlesnakes as it does not only works on their respiratory muscles, it causes muscle fasciculations (discordant contraction) and tetania (a most potent contracture of the muscles that renders a body inmobile).<br /> <br /> Enough science at that. If you are planning to rule up Nagah for the fight, i'd suggest going with the full venom potency,as in the end they are executors. But if you wanto to downgrade the damage done to vampires... may i suggest freezing them progressively (that is adding negative modifiers to their actions)? The numbers i left to you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Looking forward to seeing your results, cheesefondue. I loved your vampire vs werewolf series. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T17:20:29-08:00","id":777981,"title":"","content":"Personally I wouldn't have it do any damage to a vampire. Perhaps make them feel queasy or sick, but not to any impairment. Venom works in a very specific way that harms living things, but shouldn't have any effect on a corpse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-02T12:09:34-08:00","id":778506,"title":"","content":"Well, we're talking about supernatural venom and corpses that walk around and well, live (un-live) xD Anyway, i respect your position <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}